Here's the structured goal model based on the mission description:

### Goal Model Table

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|--------|------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|
| G1     | Fulfill Resource Request | Ensure resources are collected and delivered. | - | Achieve | - |
| G2     | Collection Phase | Collect resources from storage. | ; | Perform | G1 |
| G3     | Reach Storage | Navigate to the storage location. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G4     | Request Resources | Send request to storage for specific resources. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G5     | Wait for Retrieval | Wait until resources are retrieved. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G6     | Delivery Phase | Deliver collected resources. | ; | Perform | G1 |
| G7     | Transport Resources | Move resources to the delivery location. | - | Perform | G6 |
| G8     | Handle Low Battery (Delivery) | Return resources to a checkpoint if battery is low. | - | Perform | G6 |
| G9     | Ensure Resource Delivery | Trigger alert if resource return fails. | - | Achieve | G1 |

### Task Model Table

| Task ID | Task Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|------|----------|----------|-------------------|---------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage | Move to the storage location. | AND | Storage Area | 1 | Single robot per storage. |
| AT2     | Send Request | Transmit resource request to storage. | AND | Storage Area | 1 | Ensures correct resources are retrieved. |
| AT3     | Wait for Retrieval | Wait until resources are ready. | AND | Storage Area | 1 | Sequential after request. |
| AT4     | Navigate to Delivery Point | Transport resources to destination. | AND | Delivery Location | 1 | Single robot per delivery run. |
| AT5     | Return to Checkpoint | Bring resources back if battery low. | AND | Checkpoint | 1 | Ensures resource safety. |
| AT6     | Trigger Alert | Send notification on failure. | AND | Control Center | 1 | Critical for system integrity. |

### Logical Relationships and Justifications

- **G1 -> G2, G6**: OR (Parallel)  
  Justification: Multiple robots can collect and deliver in parallel, reducing mission time.

- **G2 -> G3, G4, G5**: AND (Sequential)  
  Justification: Collection requires sequential steps: reaching storage, requesting, then waiting.

- **G6 -> G7, G8**: AND (Sequential)  
  Justification: Delivery involves transporting and handling battery issues sequentially.

- **G8 -> AT5**: AND  
  Justification: Returning resources is a necessary step before triggering an alert.

This model ensures efficient resource management with parallel execution where possible and sequential steps where necessary, maintaining system integrity through fallback mechanisms.
